<title>USA: U.S. Stockpile sells 23.4 million lbs of rubber.</title>
<headline>U.S. Stockpile sells 23.4 million lbs of rubber.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Defense National Stockpile Center said it sold 23,412,426 pounds of technically specified heava rubber for $9,060,300.</p>
<p>Intertex World Resources bought 291,550 lbs at 32.25 cents a lb, with the rest sold to Cargill Inc at 38.78 cents a lb.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212-859-1646))</p>
</text>
